@startuml Real-Time Attendance Update
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Figure 4.4 - Real-Time Attendance Update Flow

actor "Student" as Student
participant "Student\nBrowser" as StudentUI
participant "Backend API\n(Express)" as API
participant "PostgreSQL\n(Supabase)" as DB
participant "Socket.io\nServer" as Socket
participant "Teacher\nDashboard" as TeacherUI

== Student marks attendance ==
Student -> StudentUI : Scan QR code
StudentUI -> StudentUI : Decode token\nGet GPS location
StudentUI -> API : POST /api/attendance/mark\n{ qrToken, latitude, longitude }
API -> API : Validate JWT
API -> API : Validate QR token\nCheck session ACTIVE
API -> DB : Check enrollment\nCheck duplicate
API -> API : Haversine distance\nWithin radius?
API -> DB : INSERT Attendance

== Backend notifies teacher in real time ==
API -> Socket : emit('new-attendance', data)
note right of Socket
  Room: classId or sessionId
  Data: { studentName, status, markedAt }
end note

Socket -> TeacherUI : WebSocket push\n'new-attendance' event
TeacherUI -> TeacherUI : Update live list\nNo page refresh

API --> StudentUI : 200 OK\n{ success, attendance }
StudentUI -> Student : Show "Attendance marked"

== Optional: QR refresh ==
participant "Teacher\nSession View" as TeacherSession
TeacherSession -> Socket : join room (classId)
Socket -> TeacherSession : qr-refreshed (new token)
TeacherSession -> TeacherSession : Re-render QR code

@enduml
